# Backend note: the host's own chat on the list

The list pins the host's chat, its name and its icon on this device
(`localStorage` key `wlp-own-chat`). Nothing here is written to production.

When the backend can store it, a host read should return:

- the chat id
- the title the host gave it
- the icon (an emoji, a colour, a photo url, or the initial)
- the public path `/c/<token>`, which the share button already prefers
  when `own_chat.link.path` is present

Until that read exists, the share button builds `origin + /c/` plus the
local id, and the row stays on this device.
